    "['aggregated-ether-options minimum-links [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface Port-channel1', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface Port-channel1\\n  port-channel min-links 1\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Cisco, LACP bundle interfaces are called \"Port-channel\" instead of \"aggregated ethernet (ae)\"\\n2. The command maintains the same functionality of requiring at least 1 active member link to keep the bundle operational\\n3. The Port-channel number (1) is arbitrarily chosen since Juniper\\'s ae1 doesn\\'t directly translate - you would use the same number consistently across all member interfaces in the actual configuration', 'trans_template': 'interface Port-channel1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'port-channel min-links 1', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface Port-channel1\\n  port-channel min-links 1\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Cisco, LACP bundle interfaces are called \"Port-channel\" instead of \"aggregated ethernet (ae)\"\\n2. The command maintains the same functionality of requiring at least 1 active member link to keep the bundle operational\\n3. The Port-channel number (1) is arbitrarily chosen since Juniper\\'s ae1 doesn\\'t directly translate - you would use the same number consistently across all member interfaces in the actual configuration', 'trans_template': 'port-channel min-links 1'}]]": 1,
